  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1408.02 Designation of Time Adjustment Factors",
  "priorExpiration": "1996-12-22",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1408.02 Designation of Time Adjustment Factors.\n\n(a) In order to account for differing effects of certain chemicals over time, the department shall designate a time adjustment factor according to the characteristics of the RTAP, as described in Env-A 1408.03.\n\n(b) The time adjustment factor shall be used to determine the AAL as specified in Env-A 1409.02.\n\nSource. #6328, INTERIM, eff 8-24-96, EXPIRED: 12-22-96\n\nNew. #6468-B, eff 3-5-97; ss and moved by #8278, eff 2-4-05 (from Env-A 1409.02); ss by #9601, eff 11-25-09; ss by #12443, eff 1-5-18; ss by #13334, eff 2-3-22 (formerly Env-A 1408.01)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1400.html"
